WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.921
Episode 12
Shura

00:37.746 --> 00:40.832
I've been to see your daughter, Taren.

00:41.541 --> 00:43.334
Are you an assassin from Aureatia?

00:49.466 --> 00:50.633
Is Curte all right?

00:52.302 --> 00:54.095
I wanted to save her.

00:54.846 --> 00:56.097
I was too late.

00:56.598 --> 00:57.599
I see.

00:58.224 --> 01:00.643
Let me ask you for your daughter's sake,

01:00.643 --> 01:02.437
Taren the Guarded.

01:02.437 --> 01:03.980
Why did you do it?

01:05.023 --> 01:06.649
Why did you start a war?

01:07.650 --> 01:11.029
To rule the world in place of Aureatia.

01:11.029 --> 01:12.322
Does that satisfy you?

01:12.781 --> 01:16.451
A country that relies on mercenaries
and wyverns for military strength

01:16.451 --> 01:18.495
would never last long.

01:18.495 --> 01:21.706
History provides
countless examples of rulers

01:21.706 --> 01:23.708
who were driven mad by ambition.

01:24.501 --> 01:26.961
That may be true, but...

01:28.046 --> 01:33.551
Didn't you plan all this with the leaders
of Aureatia from the very start?

01:35.929 --> 01:37.430
Wasn't this battle designed to gather

01:37.430 --> 01:41.351
all the monsters
that became a threat to the world

01:41.351 --> 01:45.230
after the True Demon King died,
and have them destroy each other?

01:46.523 --> 01:50.860
Suppose you were right,
I would never tell you.

01:51.236 --> 01:52.445
Okay,

01:52.445 --> 01:56.282
even I think
I'm being naive when I ask this...

01:56.908 --> 02:00.495
This country allowed
wyverns and minian races to coexist.

02:01.454 --> 02:03.039
Was that for your daughter's sake?

02:04.582 --> 02:05.583
No.

02:08.378 --> 02:10.797
It was all for the sake of military power.

02:10.797 --> 02:13.424
To make the wyverns obey me,

02:13.424 --> 02:14.801
I needed Curte.

02:14.801 --> 02:17.303
That may have been the case at the start,

02:17.303 --> 02:20.390
but doesn't Curte mean more to you now?

02:23.768 --> 02:25.061
Your time is nearly up.

02:28.273 --> 02:30.316
I am a holy knight.

02:30.316 --> 02:31.651
This is your confession.

02:32.485 --> 02:34.487
If you have any last words, I will listen.

02:35.113 --> 02:37.740
Last words...

02:50.587 --> 02:53.006
I want a Hero.

02:54.716 --> 02:59.470
Someone that shows there is indeed
a power stronger than fear in this world.

02:59.470 --> 03:01.806
Someone who gives the people hope.

03:01.806 --> 03:03.683
A True Hero.

03:05.977 --> 03:07.645
This is a surprise.

03:07.645 --> 03:11.649
I never thought I'd hear
the self-proclaimed Demon King say that.

03:12.442 --> 03:14.861
I've been living in fear
this whole time too,

03:14.861 --> 03:16.279
holy knight.

03:16.988 --> 03:18.281
I see.

03:18.281 --> 03:19.782
Then I'm glad.

03:20.742 --> 03:24.913
I can grant your daughter her final wish.

03:24.913 --> 03:26.414
Mom...

03:27.582 --> 03:29.500
My mom...

03:30.585 --> 03:34.422
"Please save my mom." That was her wish.

03:54.859 --> 03:55.944
There's no way

03:56.736 --> 03:59.364
this professor would do
anything to hurt you.

03:59.364 --> 04:02.784
I'm sorry. It's because I hesitated.

04:02.784 --> 04:04.619
That's why this happened to your city.

04:04.619 --> 04:06.496
Next time, I promise I'll...

04:07.580 --> 04:08.998
S-Stay back!

04:12.210 --> 04:13.294
I...

04:13.878 --> 04:14.963
I...

04:16.089 --> 04:18.299
Lana!

04:28.017 --> 04:29.102
Is this...

04:29.727 --> 04:33.439
Is this the way things are
now the True Demon King is dead?

04:34.899 --> 04:36.693
The True Demon King is dead.

04:37.235 --> 04:38.319
And yet...

04:40.697 --> 04:43.199
<i>those monsters are still here.</i>

04:45.326 --> 04:48.830
W-Who can defeat those things?

04:49.414 --> 04:51.291
There's nothing we can do...?

04:53.668 --> 04:57.964
Now it's like...
the Demon King... is everywhere!

04:57.964 --> 05:00.091
When will the fear end?

05:13.104 --> 05:14.355
No...

05:26.784 --> 05:29.078
When? When did someone get me?

05:32.915 --> 05:36.127
Life Arts... A slow-acting poison?

05:36.753 --> 05:37.754
Elea...

05:42.425 --> 05:44.927
I'm scared. So scared.

05:45.511 --> 05:47.013
We're heading towards destruction.

05:47.638 --> 05:49.515
What are we all

05:50.099 --> 05:52.185
supposed to do?

05:54.103 --> 05:57.065
What are we supposed to do?

05:58.107 --> 06:00.526
What are we supposed...

06:07.367 --> 06:08.368
There are many casualties here.

06:08.368 --> 06:09.577
Checks are complete.

06:09.577 --> 06:11.037
Roger that.
Over here!

06:11.662 --> 06:13.289
Most of the citizens have been evacuated.

06:13.289 --> 06:15.041
Watch out for leftover fighters.

06:15.041 --> 06:17.168
Especially any surviving wyverns.

06:25.468 --> 06:27.929
That's one grim expression, old man.

06:29.472 --> 06:33.810
I thought we might be in trouble
when we got hit by the Cold Star,

06:34.394 --> 06:37.313
but to think it all ended before dawn.

06:38.564 --> 06:40.316
How many citizens were killed?

06:40.316 --> 06:43.027
Excluding those caught up in the fires,

06:43.569 --> 06:45.822
I'd say not many for a war.

06:46.406 --> 06:48.032
We'll portray the series of battles

06:48.032 --> 06:50.159
as a rampage by Taren and the wyvern army,

06:50.159 --> 06:54.747
and an overreaction to this
by some of the Mage City soldiers

06:54.747 --> 06:56.332
who faced the assault.

06:57.417 --> 07:00.670
Aureatia will intervene under the guise
of a post-war recovery effort,

07:00.670 --> 07:03.005
promptly integrating Lithia
into Aureatia territory.

07:03.506 --> 07:06.092
Any political issues
will eventually be resolved.

07:06.843 --> 07:09.345
The end of the New Principality.

07:09.929 --> 07:10.930
Right.

07:10.930 --> 07:14.767
Lithia will perish
now that it has lost Taren.

07:14.767 --> 07:15.852
Still,

07:15.852 --> 07:18.604
why did the fires suddenly go out?

07:35.455 --> 07:36.998
I never thought this would happen.

07:37.582 --> 07:39.167
What will happen to Lithia?

07:39.167 --> 07:40.877
What about Master Taren?

07:40.877 --> 07:41.961
Professor?

07:42.503 --> 07:43.588
Yes, Kia?

07:45.673 --> 07:46.799
What is it?

07:47.717 --> 07:49.635
I was thinking...

07:49.635 --> 07:51.512
When I finish my studies in Aureatia,

07:52.096 --> 07:54.265
and return to Eta, then...

07:58.019 --> 07:59.604
It doesn't matter actually.

08:06.068 --> 08:07.403
The truth is...

08:08.821 --> 08:10.907
I could have helped a lot more.

08:11.824 --> 08:14.785
I'm invincible, and I can do anything.

08:15.369 --> 08:18.122
Even when facing such fires and battles...

08:18.664 --> 08:20.625
And people getting hurt and dying...

08:21.876 --> 08:24.712
No matter what terrible, sad thing I face,

08:24.712 --> 08:28.049
I should be able to beat anything.

08:28.758 --> 08:30.968
None of this is your fault, Kia.

08:30.968 --> 08:32.053
I know that.

08:32.762 --> 08:34.639
<i>Even the World Word</i>

08:34.639 --> 08:36.807
<i>is no match for some things.</i>

08:38.059 --> 08:41.395
<i>She may be an almighty being
who can defeat enemies with a single word.</i>

08:41.896 --> 08:43.814
<i>But Kia is still a young girl,</i>

08:44.357 --> 08:46.901
<i>not merely a powerful weapon.</i>

08:48.110 --> 08:50.029
<i>Before the competition starts,</i>

08:50.029 --> 08:53.407
<i>I mustn't let anybody
find out the truth about Kia.</i>

08:54.283 --> 08:56.786
<i>Someone must continue to protect her.</i>

08:58.412 --> 09:00.122
<i>I know Kia and I can win.</i>

09:00.623 --> 09:02.500
<i>No matter what trials we face.</i>

09:02.500 --> 09:04.710
<i>No matter what sins I must commit,</i>

09:04.710 --> 09:07.672
<i>I'll make sure
the World Word keeps winning.</i>

09:08.798 --> 09:09.840
Professor,

09:10.299 --> 09:12.426
you're not mad at Lana, are you?

09:12.426 --> 09:14.387
Of course not.

09:14.387 --> 09:15.930
Why would I be?

09:15.930 --> 09:19.559
In the end, she ran away like that.

09:20.017 --> 09:25.147
So I thought
if you're mad at her for that,

09:25.773 --> 09:28.234
then we could stop off at Lithia
on the way back

09:28.776 --> 09:30.903
and you could make up with her.

09:31.487 --> 09:32.572
Well...

09:39.412 --> 09:42.164
Yes, I'd love to.

09:42.164 --> 09:43.958
Do you promise?

09:43.958 --> 09:45.501
Yes, it's a promise.

09:46.460 --> 09:48.796
From now, I'll make sure I keep

09:49.297 --> 09:50.673
the promise I made to you.

09:51.340 --> 09:55.761
So teach me the right way to use my power.

09:58.764 --> 09:59.807
Of course.

09:59.807 --> 10:02.685
Let's stick together wherever we go, Kia.

10:08.357 --> 10:12.486
The Day After the Unrest

10:28.169 --> 10:29.837
Hello there, grave keeper.

10:29.837 --> 10:31.589
Need a helping hand?

10:31.589 --> 10:33.966
Thanks, I'd appreciate that.

10:34.800 --> 10:36.677
We've got yesterday's huge blaze

10:36.677 --> 10:38.554
and the wyvern attack to blame for this.

10:38.554 --> 10:42.308
A lot of soldiers died.

10:42.308 --> 10:44.018
Poor things.

10:56.822 --> 11:00.951
Those bodies look like Mage City soldiers.

11:00.951 --> 11:02.119
Right.

11:02.119 --> 11:05.706
Once you're dead, it doesn't matter
if you fought for Mage or Lithia.

11:05.706 --> 11:08.584
The same goes for the wyverns
they're burning in the square.

11:09.585 --> 11:14.090
Just until yesterday, they were soldiers
who protected this country.

11:16.050 --> 11:17.593
I agree.

11:17.593 --> 11:20.971
Truth is, nobody ought to die.

11:20.971 --> 11:23.557
Amen to that.

11:24.225 --> 11:26.435
The great Wordmaker doesn't lift a finger

11:26.435 --> 11:29.146
to help at times like this.

11:32.191 --> 11:33.609
<i>He's right.</i>

11:35.111 --> 11:37.530
<i>That's why I have to</i>

11:37.530 --> 11:39.740
<i>try and save people myself.</i>

11:41.200 --> 11:43.244
<i>As best I can.</i>

11:47.832 --> 11:49.542
Do you want to be saved?

11:51.085 --> 11:53.254
What would it take?
- Huh?

11:53.254 --> 11:55.381
For everyone to be saved.

11:55.381 --> 11:58.676
After working
as a grave keeper for so long,

11:58.676 --> 12:02.596
I often find myself wondering
the same thing as you, young man.

12:02.596 --> 12:03.764
But in the end,

12:03.764 --> 12:07.059
people can only save

12:07.059 --> 12:09.729
what they're capable of saving.

12:12.565 --> 12:13.816
Right.

12:14.358 --> 12:15.693
Absolutely.

12:15.693 --> 12:17.236
You're absolutely right.

12:22.700 --> 12:25.703
I want a Hero.

12:25.703 --> 12:28.164
<i>Would the True Hero</i>

12:28.164 --> 12:33.210
<i>have been able to save everything
without any bloodshed or tragedy?</i>

12:35.337 --> 12:37.923
<i>I want to ask them myself.</i>

12:39.049 --> 12:42.970
Ishura
Hero

12:42.970 --> 12:45.973
Can't you fix this with your Word Arts?

12:45.973 --> 12:48.851
This is my best shirt.

12:48.851 --> 12:52.354
It can probably be fixed
if we go to a big city.

12:53.439 --> 12:55.441
Won't you ride the carriage?

12:55.441 --> 12:56.692
I told you,

12:56.692 --> 12:57.860
I hate vehicles.

12:57.860 --> 13:00.821
Soujirou, I know
it's a bit late to ask this,

13:00.821 --> 13:03.783
but are you sure choosing me back then
was a good idea?

13:04.450 --> 13:07.119
Aureatia's plan
seems to have been successful,

13:07.119 --> 13:10.289
but Lord Hidow's orders
were to assassinate Taren.

13:10.915 --> 13:12.625
So, there's a chance

13:12.625 --> 13:15.836
that you won't be able to take part
in the Imperial Competition.

13:15.836 --> 13:18.130
It really is too late to worry about that.

13:18.130 --> 13:19.507
I know.

13:19.507 --> 13:21.091
It really is.

13:21.091 --> 13:22.760
Well, who cares?

13:22.760 --> 13:25.137
I had fun fighting Dakai.

13:26.597 --> 13:29.225
I only do what I choose to do,

13:29.225 --> 13:30.810
and I never regret my choices.

13:31.268 --> 13:34.396
I certainly don't need you butting in.

13:35.189 --> 13:37.733
Dakai the Magpie

13:37.733 --> 13:39.860
said something similar, didn't he?

13:40.486 --> 13:43.864
That he didn't care about
what anybody else thought.

13:43.864 --> 13:45.324
Huh?

13:46.534 --> 13:49.703
I can't forgive
that kind of thing after all.

13:49.703 --> 13:51.789
Oh, is that so?

13:52.414 --> 13:55.584
I can't stand
that the people who change our world...

13:56.043 --> 13:58.879
don't even care to look at us.

14:01.173 --> 14:04.426
I can't stand that our existence,
and the lives we've lived

14:04.426 --> 14:08.764
are treated like they don't matter,
treated like something worthless.

14:09.223 --> 14:10.349
I can't stand it.

14:10.933 --> 14:12.560
And you, Soujirou,

14:12.560 --> 14:15.896
you only care about yourself
and the person you're fighting, right?

14:15.896 --> 14:17.064
Is that bad?

14:17.648 --> 14:20.693
It's not about being bad or wrong.

14:21.443 --> 14:22.820
I can't forgive it,

14:23.404 --> 14:24.989
because the world is not something

14:24.989 --> 14:26.782
that doesn't matter.

14:33.289 --> 14:34.707
You might be right.

14:35.624 --> 14:37.668
But how would I know?

14:38.377 --> 14:40.963
I was kicked out of my last world.

14:41.505 --> 14:43.799
I only just got here
and I don't know about anything.

14:44.550 --> 14:46.594
All I know

14:46.594 --> 14:49.555
is how to swing this sword,
and how to kill.

14:50.764 --> 14:53.726
I told you when we first met,
didn't I?

14:53.726 --> 14:55.728
I said I'd guide you.

14:55.728 --> 14:58.647
Around this world,
and to the Imperial Competition.

14:59.523 --> 15:01.483
So you teach me too.

15:01.483 --> 15:02.902
Teach you what exactly?

15:02.902 --> 15:04.028
Well,

15:04.028 --> 15:06.196
let's see...

15:06.196 --> 15:09.283
You can teach me
about the Distant World you came from.

15:26.091 --> 15:27.301
So she's dead.

15:31.639 --> 15:33.265
Now you've gone and died,

15:33.891 --> 15:37.186
even I can't grant your request.

15:38.354 --> 15:39.772
Sorry about that, Nihilo.

15:41.065 --> 15:45.444
If you win the war,
you'll grant my request, won't you?

15:45.444 --> 15:49.281
Joining the minian races
one more time, huh?

15:53.243 --> 15:57.289
The minian races... They aren't so great.

16:07.007 --> 16:09.176
I knew it. You're still around.

16:14.181 --> 16:16.684
You're an Aureatian general, aren't you?

16:17.768 --> 16:20.187
A big shot, just like Harghent.

16:20.187 --> 16:23.482
I'm a civil official, not a general.

16:23.482 --> 16:25.567
I suppose you've come for this,

16:25.567 --> 16:26.694
Star Runner.

16:27.653 --> 16:30.364
Seeing as you survived the fighting,

16:30.364 --> 16:32.574
I knew you'd come for this.

16:33.200 --> 16:35.619
You could kill me and take it,

16:35.619 --> 16:37.454
but why don't we make a deal?

16:38.330 --> 16:39.665
I don't need it.

16:40.165 --> 16:42.793
The Cold Star isn't what I'm after.

16:44.586 --> 16:47.047
Then why have you followed me here?

16:47.673 --> 16:49.883
If you planned to kill me from the start,

16:49.883 --> 16:54.013
you could have just shot me in the head
from the sky, without coming down.

16:55.305 --> 16:56.724
I've heard about it.

16:57.433 --> 16:59.977
Aureatia is planning
a big Imperial Competition, right?

17:01.103 --> 17:04.940
A competition to decide a Hero,
the True Hero.

17:04.940 --> 17:06.025
That's right.

17:07.026 --> 17:08.110
I'll take part.

17:08.569 --> 17:10.529
I'll fight Harghent.

17:10.529 --> 17:12.990
What a coincidence,

17:12.990 --> 17:16.493
I was just about to suggest
the same thing.

17:17.077 --> 17:18.579
You put on that huge display

17:18.579 --> 17:22.916
because you knew
that nobody would recognize you

17:22.916 --> 17:24.460
among the swarm of wyvern soldiers.

17:25.169 --> 17:27.129
You calculated everything,

17:27.129 --> 17:29.548
allowing the Twenty-Nine Officials
of Aureatia

17:29.548 --> 17:33.385
to endorse you,
all while not revealing your trump card.

17:35.220 --> 17:37.598
A wyvern with a sharp mind.

17:37.598 --> 17:40.142
You're not called the strongest Rogue
for nothing.

17:41.185 --> 17:42.269
What's your answer?

17:42.269 --> 17:44.646
I will endorse you.

17:44.646 --> 17:46.607
The first candidate

17:47.191 --> 17:48.233
is you.

17:52.654 --> 17:55.741
One Year Earlier

17:55.741 --> 17:58.952
Aureatia Central Assembly Hall

18:00.829 --> 18:02.915
That concludes the report.

18:02.915 --> 18:06.502
There is nobody
who can confirm its validity.

18:06.835 --> 18:07.836
Once again,

18:07.836 --> 18:10.506
those who have come forward are probably
self-proclaimed heroes seeking fame.

18:10.506 --> 18:13.175
I understand. You may go.

18:13.175 --> 18:14.968
We shall continue investigations.

18:16.136 --> 18:19.181
Minia
Third Minister: Jelki the Swift Ink

18:21.016 --> 18:23.310
The era
of the self-proclaimed Demon King is over.

18:23.310 --> 18:24.937
Does a self-proclaimed Hero come next?

18:25.521 --> 18:28.273
<i>Could it be that the Hero died
without anybody knowing?</i>

18:28.774 --> 18:31.443
<i>Given the power of the True Demon King,</i>

18:31.443 --> 18:33.946
<i>it's highly likely.</i>

18:36.240 --> 18:39.368
You look as angry as usual.

18:39.368 --> 18:40.661
Are you okay?

18:41.453 --> 18:42.621
Yuca.

18:42.621 --> 18:44.957
It's nothing. Just this Hero matter.

18:44.957 --> 18:47.251
My face is the same as always.

18:47.251 --> 18:51.255
Then I take it
a Hero still hasn't been found, as always.

18:53.632 --> 18:55.259
Have you been instructed

18:55.259 --> 18:57.511
to suppress the rebels again?

18:57.511 --> 18:59.388
Is that why you're wearing armor?

18:59.388 --> 19:00.597
Hmm...

19:00.597 --> 19:02.724
Actually, that's right.

19:02.724 --> 19:04.434
I had to kill two of them.

19:05.060 --> 19:06.770
It's not a pleasant feeling.

19:06.770 --> 19:09.398
The war with the Demon King Army is over,

19:09.398 --> 19:11.859
but now I'm fighting my fellow minians.

19:11.859 --> 19:14.361
It was minian races
that fought for the Demon King Army.

19:14.361 --> 19:16.947
Well, that's true.

19:16.947 --> 19:19.074
It was just a figure of speech.

19:19.074 --> 19:21.326
You know what I mean.

19:22.744 --> 19:25.455
Yuca, about the Hero matter... Uh?

19:27.541 --> 19:28.750
Third Minister.

19:29.376 --> 19:33.088
I see this Hero matter
is still troubling you.

19:33.088 --> 19:35.215
It is a matter that doesn't concern you,

19:35.215 --> 19:36.592
Seventeenth Minister.

19:37.134 --> 19:41.471
I heard a rumor that your troops
tortured a Lithia soldier recently.

19:42.097 --> 19:45.559
Why has a woman like you
lured Her Majesty out here?

19:45.559 --> 19:47.394
What are you trying to persuade her to do?

19:47.394 --> 19:50.272
How presumptuous of you.

19:50.272 --> 19:54.693
Her Majesty herself requested
my company for a walk just now.

19:54.693 --> 19:56.195
I see.

19:56.195 --> 19:59.114
I take back what I said
about you luring Her Majesty out.

19:59.114 --> 20:00.449
Come now.

20:00.449 --> 20:02.868
We mustn't argue in a place like this.

20:02.868 --> 20:04.161
Right, Your Majesty?

20:04.161 --> 20:05.412
That's right.

20:05.412 --> 20:06.580
Jelki.

20:06.580 --> 20:08.874
The Hero is out there somewhere, right?

20:10.417 --> 20:12.753
I pray that they are.

20:12.753 --> 20:14.922
Then why haven't we found them?

20:15.505 --> 20:18.592
There are still places
that haven't been searched.

20:18.592 --> 20:19.718
It's possible

20:19.718 --> 20:21.720
that the Hero might not even be a minia.

20:21.720 --> 20:23.931
We will search the entire world.

20:24.556 --> 20:26.308
What do you think, Elea?

20:26.308 --> 20:30.687
Even if there is no Hero,
we have you, Queen Sephite.

20:31.271 --> 20:34.149
Although you are not yet involved
in governmental affairs,

20:34.733 --> 20:38.028
you will become capable
of governing the people in time.

20:38.612 --> 20:41.323
I, Elea the Red Tag,
can assure you of that.

20:41.323 --> 20:43.659
<i>That time is yet to come.</i>

20:43.659 --> 20:45.869
<i>Her Majesty is still too young now.</i>

20:45.869 --> 20:48.830
<i>The country could end up divided
at this rate.</i>

20:49.414 --> 20:52.000
Yuca, I'd like to hear your opinion too.

20:52.000 --> 20:53.710
Hmm...

20:54.211 --> 20:58.048
If the Hero did appear,
it certainly wouldn't be a bad thing.

20:58.048 --> 21:01.510
After all, they saved every one of us.

21:01.510 --> 21:03.470
Then let's find them.

21:03.470 --> 21:06.265
We just need to offer
honor and a reward, right?

21:06.265 --> 21:10.185
We've offered plenty of that up to now.

21:10.185 --> 21:13.063
Yet the True Hero still hasn't appeared.

21:13.063 --> 21:14.731
Do we need the true one?

21:14.731 --> 21:16.358
What do you mean?

21:16.358 --> 21:18.026
Does it have to be the True Hero?

21:19.528 --> 21:21.405
How about issuing a decree

21:21.405 --> 21:22.781
to decide a Hero?

21:22.781 --> 21:27.286
You mean to inform the nation
that we are searching for the Hero?

21:27.286 --> 21:28.412
Yes.

21:28.412 --> 21:31.081
If the Hero still doesn't come forward,

21:31.081 --> 21:33.792
they probably won't
even after we decide on a new Hero.

21:35.294 --> 21:36.503
In that case,

21:36.503 --> 21:39.756
why not gather the self-proclaimed heroes
who have approached Jelki

21:39.756 --> 21:42.342
and have them take part
in the Royal Games?

21:42.342 --> 21:44.803
We can bill it like,
"The strongest is the True Hero."

21:44.803 --> 21:45.887
Yuca.

21:46.471 --> 21:48.390
Does that sound too barbaric?

21:48.390 --> 21:50.058
Okay, scrap that.

21:54.062 --> 21:55.147
Jelki?

21:55.147 --> 21:58.025
Excuse me,
I was just thinking about something.

21:58.025 --> 22:00.152
Your Majesty, I shall take my leave.

22:08.618 --> 22:10.704
Take care, Jelki.

22:11.204 --> 22:12.456
<i>Somebody...</i>

22:13.123 --> 22:15.500
<i>Somebody has to make this happen.</i>

22:18.962 --> 22:20.881
<i>We only need one Hero.</i>

22:20.881 --> 22:23.300
<i>To begin a new era,</i>

22:23.300 --> 22:26.094
<i>the monsters that could
potentially destroy the world</i>

22:26.094 --> 22:28.138
<i>must be eradicated.</i>

22:33.727 --> 22:36.438
<i>I'm the only one who can do it.</i>

22:37.981 --> 22:41.693
<i>What's needed now, is a way to it.</i>

22:56.041 --> 22:59.878
<i>The enemy of the world
that filled the horizon with fear,</i>

23:00.587 --> 23:02.547
<i>the True Demon King,</i>

23:02.547 --> 23:04.174
<i>was defeated by somebody.</i>

23:05.258 --> 23:07.177
<i>To this very day,</i>

23:07.177 --> 23:11.807
<i>that lone Hero remains unknown,
both in name and existence.</i>

23:12.599 --> 23:18.605
<i>Now the age of fear has come to an end,
that person has to be chosen.</i>

23:19.689 --> 23:22.901
<i>The</i> shura <i>now have four names.</i>

23:24.361 --> 23:26.029
<i>Alus the Star Runner.</i>

23:27.447 --> 23:29.324
<i>Kia the World Word.</i>

23:30.659 --> 23:32.911
<i>Nastique the Quiet Singer.</i>

23:34.287 --> 23:36.289
<i>Soujirou the Willow-Sword.</i>

23:38.041 --> 23:39.835
ISHURA

23:39.835 --> 23:41.920
Translated by Zacarias Hicks
